A previously developed approach by Baker achieved PTAS on various graph classes including planar graphs. Further, Romero, Wrochna, and Zivny developed a simpler PTAS for certain graph classes using a different method, which also yields almost-linear time complexity, essentially preserving efficiency.

This research is extended to provide a PTAS with an even more streamlined proof, preserving efficiency while relaxing a key assumption about the approximate nature of related problems.
